! Progressive 在 (zài)

Before many activity verbs, 在 marks an action in progress.

* 我在学中文。 — Wǒ zài xué Zhōngwén. — I'm studying Chinese.
* 他在吃饭。 — Tā zài chī fàn. — He's eating a meal.

在 can also be a verb/preposition associated with location; its function is determined by syntax.

This construction does not simply mean “present tense”: the progressive event can be located in a past time frame too.

